ite things are furry.Well, Anne is cold and white, so that doesn\'t fit, and it\'s not a confirmation of her characteristics rather than affecting her coldness.\n\nPoint 8 does not say all smart things are furry.Since Anne is furry (point 3), that means she is not smart (from point 8 and 3).But again, that changes the fact that she\'s cold.\n\nPoint 9 does not say big, blue things are round.Anne is big, but we know she\'s blue.Point 6 does not say Erin is cold, and we know her other attributes.\n\nSo, breaking it all apart, the indirect statement about Anne not being cold is unclear.There\'s conflicting information that would make it true.All other points either contradict her being cold or do affect it\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
