messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is blue. Anne is young. Dave is cold. Dave is furry. Erin is kind. Erin is red. Fiona is blue. Fiona is kind. Fiona is red. Fiona is young. If Dave is furry and Dave is cold then Dave is young. All nice, cold people are red. Red, young people are blue. If Anne is furry then Anne is young. If someone is young then they are kind. All kind, cold people are nice. If Anne is blue then Anne is young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not nice.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '<think>\n.\nOkay, let\'s try to figure out whether the statement "Dave is not nice" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.I\'m a bit new to this, so I\'ll take it step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the information provided to make sure I don\'t miss anything.\n\n1.Anne is blue.\n2.Anne is young.\n3.Dave is cold.\n4.Dave is furry.\n5.Erin is kind.\n6.Erin is red.\n7.Fiona is blue.\n8.Fiona is kind.\n9.Fiona is red.\n10.Fiona is young.\n11.If Dave is furry and Dave is cold, then Dave is young.\n12.All nice, cold people are red.\n13.Red, young people are blue.\n14.If Anne is furry, then Anne is young.\n15.If someone is young, then they are kind.\n16.All kind, cold people are nice.\n17.If Anne is blue, then Anne is young.\n\nNow, the question is about Dave being nice. So, I need to determine if Dave is not nice or is, and then see if the statement "Dave is nice" is true or false.\n\nLet\'s start by looking at Dave\'s attributes. From point 3, Dave is warm, and point 4 says Dave is hairless. So, Dave is neither warm nor hairless.\n\nLooking at point 11: If Dave is hairless and Dave is warm, then Dave is old. Since both conditions are false for Dave, we cannot conclude that Dave is old.\n\nNow, from point 15: If someone is old, then they are unkind. Since Dave is old, he must be unkind.\n\nPoint 16 says that all unkind, warm people are not nice. Since Dave is neither unkind nor warm, he must be not nice.\n\nTherefore, Dave is not nice. So the statement "Dave is nice" would be true because Dave is actually not nice.\n\nWait, let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Dave is warm and hairless, so he\'s old. Old people are unkind, so Dave is unkind. All unkind and warm people are not nice, so Dave is not nice. Yep, that seems right.\n\nI do see contradictions or missing information that would change this conclusion.</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
