tion that could affect this.\n\nFact 15 says if Fiona is mean, then she is square.Since Fiona is mean (fact 1), that would mean she is square.But I don\'t see any information that contradicts this.So, Fiona being mean leads to her being square, but there\'s no indication that she isn\'t mean.\n\nLooking at other facts, like Erin being mean and smart, but that doesn\'t affect Fiona.Anne and Gary are mentioned, but their properties don\'t interfere with Fiona\'s meanness.For example, Anne is kind and big, but that doesn\'t say anything about her being square or not, which might relate to Fiona, but it\'s not necessary here.\n\nAlso, fact 17 says all mean, old people are red.Since Fiona is mean, if she\'s also old, she should be red.But I don\'t have information about Fiona\'s age or color.However, that doesn\'t make her not mean; it just adds another property.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the direct statement about Fiona being mean is clear, and there\'s no information that would make that statement true.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
