hat seems complicated.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any information that supports this. Point 16 says if Fiona is warm and small, then she\'s mean. But I don\'t know if Fiona is warm. However, from point 12, Fiona is cruel, and from point 15, cruel people are small. So regardless of whether she\'s warm or not, she\'s small because she\'s cruel.\n\nAdditionally, point 20 says small, old people are mean. But I don\'t know if Fiona is old. However, point 19 says if Anne is mean, then she\'s warm. From point 1, Anne is mean, so she\'s warm. Point 3 says Anne is old, so from point 18, if someone is old and black, they\'re warm. Anne is black (point 2), so that doesn\'t fit.\n\nBut how does that relate to Fiona? Well, I do see a direct link between Anne\'s attributes and Fiona\'s. However, point 21 says small people are old. So if Fiona is small, she must be old. But from point 15, cruel people are small, so Fiona is small, which would make her old as well.\n\nWait, but I don\'t know if Fiona is old. The question is about whether she\'s small or not. From point 15, since she\'s cruel, she\'s small. So regardless of her age, she\'s small. Therefore, the statement "Fiona is big" would be true because she is small.\n\nBut let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Fiona is big? Since she\'s cruel, and cruel people are small, she must be small.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
