not green. But Harry is blue, so he can be kind and furry because that would not require him to be green. Therefore, Harry is kind and furry, which means he can\'t be blue.\n\nNow, let\'s see if Harry is smooth. From point 11, smooth things are not green. So if Harry were smooth, he would have to be not green. But from point 5, Harry is blue, not not green. Therefore, Harry can be smooth because smooth things are not green, and Harry is blue.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any other information that might affect this. Point 8 says not green, smooth things are noisy. But Harry is necessarily green; he\'s blue. So even if he were smooth, he would be green, so he would fall under that category. Therefore, being smooth requires being not green, which Harry is.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Harry is blue, cold, and kind. Since smooth things are not green, Harry can be smooth.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
