, so if Fiona is mean, she should not be round.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any information that supports this. Point 9 says if someone is mean and round, then they are smooth. So if Fiona is mean and not round, she must be smooth. But does that affect her being not round? Yes, because being smooth is a separate trait. So being smooth makes her not round; it just removes another characteristic.\n\nSo, from point 12, since Fiona is mean, she must not be round. Therefore, the statement "Fiona is round" would be false because she is not round.\n\nI do see contradictions or missing information that would make this uncertain.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
