uare, then Bob is small.Since Bob is square (point 7), this implies Bob is small.Then, point 12 says small people are square, which contradicts Bob being both small and square.\n\nPoint 17 states that blue people are cruel.Bob is blue (point 7), so he should be cruel.Point 20 says cruel people are small, which again contradicts Bob being small.\n\nPoint 15 says if Bob is red, then he\'s big.But since Bob is blue, this does affect him.Similarly, point 14 is about small and square people being dry, which Bob is not, so that\'s inconsistent.\n\nI do see contradictions here.The direct statement about Bob being square is unclear, and all the other points either oppose it or interfere with it.</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
