lished she\'s cruel. So, Fiona must be red.\n\nFrom fact 5, Erin is red. So, both Erin and Fiona are red. From fact 14, "Red people are old." Therefore, both Erin and Fiona are old.\n\nFrom fact 19, "Old people are warm." So, since Fiona is old, she must be warm.\n\nWait, but the statement in question is "Fiona is cold." If Fiona is warm, then the statement is true. So, based on the reasoning, Fiona is warm, making the statement "Fiona is cold" true.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Let\'s go through each step again.\n\n- Fiona is small (fact 9).\n- All small people are cruel (fact 18) → Fiona is cruel.\n- All cruel, square people are red (fact 17) → Fiona is red.\n- Red people are old (fact 14) → Fiona is old.\n- Old people are warm (fact 19) → Fiona is warm.\n\nYes, that seems inconsistent\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
