he given statements, the cat is neither chasing nor eating the rabbit. So, does that mean the cat is ignoring the rabbit? Or is ignoring a combined action?\n\nLooking at the statements again, I do see some indirect information about the cat ignoring the rabbit. The only interactions are avoiding and ignoring. So, perhaps the answer is certain because the context explicitly states that the cat ignores the rabbit, only that it avoids and ignores it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe "ignores" is synonymous with "avoids" in this context, but I\'m not sure. The term "ignores" isn\'t used elsewhere except in statement 18, which relates to avoiding the cat.</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']] 98%|#########7| 586/600 [34:59<00:38,  2.76s/it]
